@@ -234,6 +236,18 @@ sees rig-scoped work beads — the `assignee` field alone does not route
 by namespace. For HQ-only refineries `$GC_RIG` is empty and the flag
 expands to nothing.
 
+**Order: priority first, then earliest first handoff (gcp-et7g).** Each query
+fetches every candidate (`--limit=0`) and picks in jq, never `--limit=1`. The
+store's default order is priority ascending, then created_at DESCENDING, so a
+server-side limit of one serves every priority band newest-first and old merge
+requests starve while new same-priority work keeps arriving (winnow, 2026-09-24:
+47 same-band overtakes, one bead waited ~9h). `--sort` cannot fix it: it takes a
+single key, and every single key drops priority. `first_submitted_at` is
+stamped by the polecat's refinery handoff and kept across rejections, so a
+resubmitted bead goes back to its original place in line rather than the back
+of the band. A bead handed over without the stamp — before the stamp existed,
+or by hand — falls back to `created_at`.
